"Path through Ravine"
"Rolling hills surround you here, the only real view off to the west down a
gully.  The grey walls of a small town are visible in the distance there,
mostly obscured by brush and stone.  Switchbacking, the trail descends into
the gully, and off further into dense bush and rock eastwards.  Further south,
a steep rocky climb leads to a hillcrest, tall branches from some tree
silhouetted behind to the southeast.
